    "output": "LEGAL MEMORANDUM — MPRDA MINING RIGHT TRANSFER\nTO: General Counsel / Executive Committee\nRE: Mining Right Acquisition — Due Diligence Framework\nCLASSIFICATION: ATTORNEY-CLIENT PRIVILEGED\n\n1. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK: Section 11 of the Mineral and Petroleum Resources Development Act 28 of 2002 governs transfer, cession, letting, subletting, assignment, or alienation of mining rights. Ministerial consent from the DMRE is mandatory. The Minister must be satisfied that the transferee has financial resources, technical ability, and complies with the Mining Charter and BEE requirements.\n\n2. TRANSFER CONDITIONS: The Minister must be satisfied that the transferee will comply with the MPRDA, the prospecting or mining work programme, and environmental management programme. The transferee must not be disqualified by previous right cancellation, unpaid royalties, or conviction under the MHSA or NEMA.\n\n3. DUE DILIGENCE RISK MATRIX:\n- Unpaid royalties or BEE non-compliance by seller: HIGH. Mitigation: escrow holdback until DMRE confirms clean status.\n- Outstanding environmental compliance order: HIGH. Mitigation: seller warranty and indemnity for pre-closing breaches.\n- Mining Charter BEE threshold (currently 30% black ownership): CRITICAL. Confirm Veralogix Group entity meets threshold or structure compliant SPV.\n- WUL / AEL non-compliance: HIGH. Environmental audit by IO Green and Bioniq pre-closing.\n- Labour retrenchment risks: MEDIUM. LRA compliance warranty; retention pool for critical staff.\n\n4. STRUCTURAL CONSIDERATIONS: Asset purchase (direct right transfer) requires Section 11 consent (6-12 months) but isolates liabilities. Share purchase is faster but inherits all historical liabilities and may trigger Ministerial notice requirements for change of control under Section 11 read with the right's terms.\n\n5. RECOMMENDED SEQUENCE: Phase 1 (Weeks 1-4): Preliminary DD on Mining Charter, royalties, environmental orders, SLP status. Phase 2 (Weeks 5-8): Definitive technical, financial, and legal DD. Phase 3 (Weeks 9-12): Transaction documents. Phase 4 (Week 13+): Section 11 application to DMRE with BEE Verification Certificate and environmental audit."
