    "output": "LEGAL MEMORANDUM — PROVISIONAL AEL SUSPENSION RESPONSE\nTO: Plant Manager / General Counsel / COO\nRE: DFFE/AEL/MPU/2026-0847 — Provisional AEL Suspension\nCLASSIFICATION: ATTORNEY-CLIENT PRIVILEGED\n\n1. ISSUE: Whether the DFFE provisional suspension can be averted through remediation, and the legal and operational pathway to restore AEL status while maintaining revenue protection.\n\n2. RULE: Under NEM: AQA, AEL is site-specific. Provisional suspension under Section 47 does not extinguish the licence but places the holder on notice. The holder has a statutory window to present a remediation plan. Operation without an AEL is a strict liability offence under Section 51 with potential director liability under Section 49B.\n\n3. APPLICATION: The 30-day remediation window is a statutory lifeline. The root cause (aging baghouse) is addressable. The DFFE responds favourably to holders who treat exceedances as systemic improvement triggers rather than mere violations. The 'Category 2 non-compliance' designation under DFFE Enforcement Policy typically attracts administrative enforcement rather than criminal liability, provided good faith and rapid remediation are demonstrated.\n\n4. RECOMMENDED STRATEGY: Phase 1 (Days 1-10): Request 60-day extension for capital-intensive remediation. Activate emergency abatement: temporary throughput reduction, baghouse compartment replacement, and Ca(OH)2 dry sorbent injection. Phase 2 (Days 11-30): Submit comprehensive remediation plan with WFGD procurement timeline, third-party audit commitment, and voluntary penalty settlement offer. Invoke Mining Charter beneficiation compliance advantage. Phase 3 (Days 31-120): Commission permanent WFGD; negotiate compliance-linked EPC contract with performance guarantees.\n\n5. CROSS-FUNCTIONAL COORDINATION: IO Green leads regulatory interface and environmental audit. Endeto Projects manages WFGD civil infrastructure. Bioniq deploys real-time monitoring. Veramani tracks capex in ERP. Vera-Commodities coordinates offtake delivery contingency. Legal manages all DFFE correspondence and preserves privilege over remediation strategy documents.\n\n6. DECISION REQUIRED: Approve R16.83m remediation capital (emergency repair R1.2m, WFGD R14.5m, audit R380k, penalty R750k) to protect R216m annual revenue stream."
