    "instruction": "Draft a legal opinion on cross-subsidiary liability when Group company A's equipment operated by contractor B damages Group company C's property.",
    "input": "Veralogix Rentals (Group company A) leased excavator to external mining contractor. Contractor damaged CPI (Group company C) processing plant conveyor during loading. CPI claims from contractor. Contractor claims indemnity from Veralogix Rentals alleging defective equipment maintenance. Need to analyse contractual and delictual liability chains.",
    "output": "LEGAL OPINION — CROSS-SUBSIDIARY LIABILITY CHAIN\nTO: General Counsel / Veralogix Rentals / CPI\nRE: Inter-Group Liability — Equipment Damage Incident\nCLASSIFICATION: ATTORNEY-CLIENT PRIVILEGED\n\n1. ISSUE: Whether Veralogix Rentals owes CPI a duty in delict or contract for damage caused by a third-party contractor operating Veralogix Rentals equipment, and whether the contractor's indemnity claim against Veralogix Rentals has legal merit.\n\n2. RULE: In the absence of a direct contract between Veralogix Rentals and CPI for this specific operation, CPI's claim against the contractor rests in delict. The contractor's claim against Veralogix Rentals depends on the rental agreement's indemnity and liability allocation clauses. Veralogix Rentals' liability to the contractor is contractual, not delictual, unless maintenance negligence is proven independently.\n\n3. APPLICATION: Assuming standard Veralogix Rentals terms: the lessee assumes liability for operational damage unless caused by Veralogix Rentals' maintenance default. The burden shifts to the contractor to prove maintenance failure caused or contributed to the damage. If maintenance records show compliance with SLA, Veralogix Rentals has strong defences against both contractor indemnity and CPI subrogation claims.\n\n4. INTER-GROUP RISK: Because Veralogix Rentals and CPI share a holding structure, insurers may treat this as an intra-group loss for deductible purposes. However, for legal liability analysis, each subsidiary is a separate juristic person unless a Group guarantee or inter-company services agreement modifies the position.\n\n5. RECOMMENDED ACTIONS: (a) Preserve all maintenance records and operator training documentation for the unit. (b) Engage loss assessor jointly if insurance overlap exists. (c) Review inter-company services agreement between Rentals and CPI for risk allocation clauses. (d) If contractor indemnity claim proceeds, ensure discovery extends to contractor's loading procedures, operator certification, and site supervision records. (e) Consider amending future rental agreements to strengthen lessee liability for operational damage and exclude liability for consequential damage to Group affiliates."
