    "input": "Standard dry lease agreement for Mahindra HDX-320XR excavator. Lessee: external mining contractor. 12-month term. Monthly rate R580,000. Lessee responsible for daily maintenance. Veralogix Rentals responsible for major overhauls. Limitation of liability clause caps at12 months' rental. Force majeure clause standard.",
    "output": "CONTRACT REVIEW — EQUIPMENT LEASE AGREEMENT\nTO: Veralogix Rentals / General Counsel\nRE: Standard Dry Lease — Mahindra HDX-320XR\nCLASSIFICATION: ATTORNEY-CLIENT PRIVILEGED\n\n1. POSITIVE PROVISIONS: Lessee daily maintenance obligation is standard and appropriate. Veralogix Rentals retains major overhaul responsibility, protecting brand and asset value. 12-month term provides revenue predictability.\n\n2. RISK AREAS:\n- Limitation of liability cap at 12 months' rental (R6.96m) may be inadequate for catastrophic damage scenarios where the excavator is destroyed or causes third-party property damage exceeding the cap. Recommend tiered liability: cap applies to equipment damage only, with uncapped or higher limit for third-party bodily injury and property damage.\n- Force majeure clause should explicitly exclude 'mining market downturn' and 'commodity price fluctuation' from force majeure events. These are commercial risks standardly borne by lessees in mining equipment rental.\n- No minimum hours/utilization guarantee. If lessee under-utilises, Veralogix Rentals bears the opportunity cost. Recommend minimum monthly hours clause with shortfall payments.\n- Insurance: Verify lessee maintains all-risk insurance naming Veralogix Rentals as loss payee and additional insured. Confirm public liability insurance limits are appropriate for mining environment (suggest minimum R50m).\n- Default and remedy: Recommend reducing cure period from 30 days to 7 days for payment defaults and 72 hours for maintenance defaults affecting safety-critical systems.\n- Cross-default: Link to any other agreements between Veralogix Rentals and the same lessee.\n\n3. RECOMMENDED AMENDMENTS: (a) Add performance guarantee (minimum hours). (b) Strengthen liability cap structure. (c) Add automatic equipment substitution right if maintenance downtime exceeds 48 hours. (d) Require real-time telemetry access via Smart Mining Solutions integration as contract condition."
